---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="What data this site collects and how it's used.">
  <article class="post-content">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>
      This site is static — there's no login, no account, and no server-side database. Here's
      what does happen when you visit.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <a href="https://marketingplatform.google.com/about/analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics</a>
      to understand how the site is used — which pages are read, roughly how visitors found the
      site, and general device/location information (like country and browser). This does not
      identify you personally.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics only runs if you accept the cookie banner shown on your first visit. If you
      decline, no analytics script loads and no analytics cookies are set. You can change your
      choice at any time using the "Manage cookie preferences" link in the footer.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      If you accept analytics, Google Analytics sets its own cookies to distinguish visitors.
      Separately, this site stores your accept/decline choice itself in your browser's local
      storage, so you're not asked again on every visit. Declining sets a "declined" choice; it
      does not delete anything.
    </p>

    <h2>Other third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts' CDN, which — like any external resource — receives
      your IP address and browser information as part of that request. No account or tracking
      cookie is involved.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Decline (or later withdraw) analytics consent using the cookie banner.</li>
      <li>Clear cookies and local storage in your browser at any time to reset your choice.</li>
      <li>Use a browser extension or built-in tracking protection to block analytics scripts entirely.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this policy, <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
